<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Carson returns two weeks after a left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. The germline panel before surgery showed no pathogenic variant. She asked to hear the pathology in full and had it from Dr. Solís-Abernathy last week, and again today: the cancer was 2.3 cm, grade 2, with clear margins, and two of the three sentinel lymph nodes contained cancer, without spread beyond the node capsules (pT2 pN1a, anatomic stage IIB). She was told plainly that the cancer had reached lymph nodes under the arm, that this raises the chance of it returning, and that treatment is still given with the aim of cure. The recurrence score is 17. Last week the multidisciplinary breast team (surgery, medical oncology, and radiation oncology) reviewed the results and gave her their recommendations with the expected benefits and side effects in numbers; she took a week to read about them and has decided. The urea breath test three days ago, two weeks after she stopped omeprazole, was negative. The wound has healed and she has little pain on acetaminophen. She is writing again in the mornings. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Left lumpectomy and sentinel node biopsy two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Pathology</td><td>pT2 pN1a(sn), 2 of 3 sentinel nodes, grade 2, margins clear; recurrence score 17</td></tr><tr><td>Genetics</td><td>No pathogenic germline variant</td></tr><tr><td>Her decisions</td><td>Radiation; letrozole with ribociclib; zoledronic acid; no chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Ulcer</td><td>Urea breath test negative; Helicobacter pylori eradicated</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

