<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Metastatic carcinoma in two of three left sentinel lymph nodes; pT2 pN1a(sn) M0, anatomic stage IIB (C77.3)</content>. One or two positive sentinel nodes after breast-conserving surgery that will be followed by whole-breast radiation: axillary dissection would add arm swelling without improving survival, so it is not needed. With nodal disease, radiation to the regional lymph nodes is added. Staging scans are not needed without symptoms. [S]<list><item>Hypofractionated whole-breast and regional nodal radiation with a tumor-bed boost, starting in two weeks, booked in the afternoons at her request.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left breast cancer, hormone receptor positive, HER2 negative, after lumpectomy (C50.412)</content>. Postmenopausal with one to three positive nodes and a recurrence score of 17: chemotherapy would add no meaningful benefit. Stage II node-positive disease makes her eligible for adjuvant ribociclib with an aromatase inhibitor, which in its trial lowered the risk of invasive recurrence by about 3 percentage points at three years, at the cost of fortnightly blood tests at first, ECG checks, a low white count, and rarely liver injury. She chose to take it. [S]<list><item>After radiation: letrozole 2.5 mg daily for at least five years with ribociclib 400 mg on days 1 to 21 of each 28-day cycle for three years.</item><item>Before ribociclib: ECG, blood count, liver tests, and electrolytes; a list of drugs that prolong the QT interval, to avoid.</item><item>Adjuvant zoledronic acid every six months for three years, after a dental check, with a baseline DXA.</item><item>Mammogram six to twelve months after radiation, then yearly.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Duodenal ulcer with Helicobacter pylori (K26.9)</content>. Urea breath test negative: infection eradicated and the ulcer treated. Resolved. [S]<list><item>No further acid suppression; continue to avoid nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Post-operative wound, shoulder, and arm check</td><td>After surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Wounds healed; shoulder flexion 160 degrees; no seroma</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Surgical pathology and recurrence score</td><td>After surgery</td><td>Up to date</td><td>pT2 pN1a(sn), margins clear; recurrence score 17</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Germline genetic testing</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No pathogenic variant; result given before surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Disclosure of the pathology and shared decision-making</td><td>At every result</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Pathology given in full in plain words with a copy; benefits and harms of each treatment given in numbers; decisions made by her after a week to consider them</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lymphedema assessment and risk-reduction counseling</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>25.5 cm on each side, unchanged from the pre-operative baseline; counseled on early signs</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Medical and radiation oncology</td><td>After surgery</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Seen last week at the multidisciplinary breast clinic</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT, bone scan, or PET for distant spread</td><td>Only with symptoms or clinical stage III</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Pathologic stage IIB without symptoms of spread</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Tumor markers</td><td>Not recommended for early breast cancer</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Ribociclib baseline ECG, blood count, liver tests, and electrolytes</td><td>Before the first dose</td><td>Due</td><td>At the visit when letrozole and ribociclib start, after radiation</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Baseline at aromatase inhibitor start</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked for the day letrozole starts</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dental assessment before zoledronic acid</td><td>Before the first infusion</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Dental check booked before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress, depression, and anxiety screen (PHQ-9 and GAD-7)</td><td>At periodic intervals</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 4 and GAD-7 5</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Helicobacter pylori test of cure</td><td>At least four weeks after antibiotics and two weeks off a proton pump inhibitor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Urea breath test three days ago: negative</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Receive the biopsy result in person within ten days, explained in plain words, with a copy of the report. Outcome by 2026-03-18: Told the diagnosis in person nine days after presentation, with the pathology report in hand; teach-back confirmed her understanding [S]</item><item>Make each treatment decision herself after hearing the options, benefits, and harms. Outcome by 2026-04-20: Chose breast-conserving surgery and, after the pathology, radiation, letrozole, ribociclib, and zoledronic acid [S]</item><item>Complete surgery and radiation, then start endocrine therapy, within four months of diagnosis. In progress; target 2026-06-15 [S]</item><item>Take adjuvant systemic therapy safely, with every safety check the drugs require done on schedule. In progress; target 2026-12-07 [S]</item><item>Keep writing at least four mornings a week through treatment. In progress; target 2026-12-07 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Code of Medical Ethics Opinion 2.1.3: Withholding Information from Patients (2016); Management of the Axilla in Early-Stage Breast Cancer: Ontario Health (Cancer Care Ontario) and ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2021;39(27):3056-3082 (2021); Optimal Adjuvant Chemotherapy and Targeted Therapy for Early Breast Cancer-Cyclin-Dependent Kinase 4 and 6 Inhibitors: ASCO Guideline Rapid Recommendation Update. J Clin Oncol 2024;42(18):2233-2235 (2024); Use of Adjuvant Bisphosphonates and Other Bone-Modifying Agents in Breast Cancer: ASCO-OH (CCO) Guideline Update. J Clin Oncol 2022;40(7):787-800 (2022); ACG Clinical Guideline: Treatment of Helicobacter pylori Infection. Am J Gastroenterol 2024;119(9):1730-1753 (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Radiation starting in two weeks. Primary care visit after radiation, on the day letrozole and ribociclib start. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-15: start of letrozole, ribociclib, and zoledronic acid after radiation. [S]</paragraph></text>

